---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Nexus Wave Technologies">
  <section class="hero legal-hero"><div class="container post-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy & Data Protection</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">A clear explanation of what information Nexus Wave Technologies may process, why we process it, how long we keep it, and the choices available to you.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container legal-shell"><nav class="legal-nav" aria-label="Legal pages"><a href="/legal/privacy" aria-current="page">Privacy</a><a href="/legal/terms">Terms</a><a href="/legal/refund">Refunds</a><a href="/legal/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a><a href="/legal/accessibility">Accessibility</a><a href="/account">Account</a></nav><article class="prose card legal-document">
    <h2>1. Who this policy is for</h2>
    <p>This policy applies to the Nexus Wave Technologies website, Nexus Plus, Geeta Nexus integrations, support services, community entry points, product pages and other services that link to this policy. Where a specific feature has additional privacy information, that information also applies.</p>

    <h2>2. Who is responsible for your information?</h2>
    <p>Nexus Wave Technologies is responsible for the services described here. Privacy questions and requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:info@nexusweb.co.in">info@nexusweb.co.in</a>.</p>
    <p>For people in the European Economic Area or other jurisdictions with similar rights, this policy is intended to provide the information required by applicable data-protection law. This page is general information and is not legal advice.</p>

    <h2>3. Information we may process</h2>
    <p>Depending on what you choose to use, we may process account information such as your name, email address, verified contact information and account identifiers; content you create or select such as text, notes, documents, images, audio and video; support requests and messages; payment and transaction information needed to verify purchases; device, app, network and security information; notification tokens; preferences; and information needed to operate connected features.</p>

    <h2>4. Sensitive permissions and user-started features</h2>
    <p>Nexus Plus may use permissions such as microphone, camera, media access, nearby-device or network access, notifications, contacts, phone or SMS access where a particular feature requires them. We aim to request these permissions only when needed. Features that process sensitive information should explain the purpose in the app before access is requested, and you can deny or later revoke permissions through the relevant device controls.</p>
    <p>Some accessibility or device-control features may process information that is especially sensitive. Those features are intended only for the purpose shown to you in the app and should not be used to bypass platform security or access devices or accounts without authorization.</p>

    <h2>5. Why we use information</h2>
    <p>We use information to provide requested features; authenticate and protect accounts; save settings and content; complete transactions and provide support; prevent abuse, fraud and security problems; improve reliability and compatibility; send notifications you have enabled; comply with legal obligations; and operate third-party services that you choose to use.</p>

    <h2>6. Legal bases for processing</h2>
    <p>Where GDPR or similar laws apply, processing may be based on performance of a contract, your consent, our legitimate interests where permitted, compliance with a legal obligation, or another lawful basis available under applicable law. We aim to use the least information reasonably needed for the relevant purpose.</p>

    <h2>7. Local processing and cloud processing</h2>
    <p>Some features work locally on your device. Other features may send selected content to a service provider when you ask the feature to use that provider. Before using a feature that requires external processing, the app should identify the relevant purpose and provider as required by the applicable platform and law.</p>

    <h2>8. Google Drive</h2>
    <p>Google Drive backup is optional. When enabled, supported backup data may be stored in app-specific Google Drive storage. Data prepared for cloud storage may be encrypted by the app before upload. Google processes Google Drive data under its own terms and privacy documentation.</p>

    <h2>9. Payments and paid services</h2>
    <p>Paid services may involve subscription or usage-based purchases. Payment and transaction information may be processed by the payment or app-store provider and by systems needed to verify and maintain entitlements, refunds and fraud controls. Nexus Wave Technologies does not ask you to disclose your UPI PIN, bank password, OTP or account recovery codes to us.</p>

    <h2>10. Third-party service providers</h2>
    <p>Depending on the feature, information may be processed by providers for authentication, hosting and databases, cloud storage, notifications, AI or document processing, payments, analytics or connected-device functionality. We aim to disclose material categories of providers in the app or website and to require appropriate protection where applicable.</p>

    <h2>11. Data sharing and selling</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal information to data brokers. We do not use Secure Vault secrets or other sensitive content for targeted advertising. Information may be shared with service providers when needed to deliver a requested feature, with authorities when legally required, or in a business transfer where applicable law requires appropriate notice and protections.</p>

    <h2>12. International transfers</h2>
    <p>Some service providers may process information outside your country. Where applicable law requires safeguards for international transfers, we aim to use appropriate contractual, organizational or other lawful measures.</p>

    <h2>13. Retention</h2>
    <p>We keep information only for as long as reasonably needed for the purpose for which it was collected, to provide and secure the service, to meet legal and accounting requirements, to handle disputes, or where another lawful reason requires retention. Different categories can therefore have different retention periods.</p>
    <p>Temporary files and operational records should be removed when they are no longer needed. Payment and legal records may need to be retained longer where required by law.</p>

    <h2>14. Your privacy rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights to be informed, access your information, correct it, request deletion, restrict processing, receive a portable copy, object to certain processing, withdraw consent where consent is the legal basis, and complain to a supervisory authority. You can start a request by contacting <a href="mailto:info@nexusweb.co.in">info@nexusweb.co.in</a>.</p>

    <h2>15. Account deletion</h2>
    <p>If you create a Nexus account, account deletion should be available through supported account controls. Deleting an account is intended to remove the account and associated data that we are not legally required to retain. Data held independently by a third-party service is subject to that provider's rules, and legally required records may be retained for the required period.</p>
    <p>For a direct account request, use the <a href="/account">Account</a> page when available or contact us using the email above.</p>

    <h2>16. Children</h2>
    <p>Our services are not intentionally designed to collect personal information from children in violation of applicable law. Where age-related restrictions apply, users should follow the requirements shown by the relevant store or feature.</p>

    <h2>17. Security</h2>
    <p>We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards such as encrypted connections, access controls, protected credentials, secure device storage where supported and authorization checks. No service can guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h2>18. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy when the services, data practices, providers, security measures or legal requirements change. The effective date below identifies the current version.</p>

    <h2>19. Contact and privacy requests</h2>
    <p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@nexusweb.co.in">info@nexusweb.co.in</a></p>
    <p>Website: <a href="/">Nexus Wave Technologies</a></p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: October 2, 2026.</p>
  </article></div></section>
<style is:global>
  .legal-hero{padding:72px 0 40px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border);background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--color-surface),var(--color-bg))}
  .legal-hero .lead{max-width:780px}
  .legal-shell{display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px minmax(0,1fr);gap:32px;align-items:start}
  .legal-nav{position:sticky;top:96px;display:grid;gap:6px;padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:16px;background:var(--color-surface)}
  .legal-nav a{padding:10px 12px;border-radius:10px;color:var(--color-text-muted);text-decoration:none;font-size:.92rem;font-weight:650}
  .legal-nav a:hover,.legal-nav a[aria-current=page]{background:var(--color-surface-soft);color:var(--color-text)}
  .legal-document{padding:32px}
  .legal-document h2{margin:34px 0 10px;font-size:1.35rem}
  .legal-document h2:first-child{margin-top:0}
  .legal-document p{margin:0 0 14px;color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.75}
  @media(max-width:850px){.legal-shell{grid-template-columns:1fr}.legal-nav{position:static;display:flex;overflow:auto}.legal-nav a{flex:0 0 auto}.legal-document{padding:24px}}
</style>
</Layout>